course: dictionary
lesson: 15957
title: Untangled: from knots to clear answers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Untangled is a word you can picture. Imagine string twisted into knots. Someone works the knots out, one loop at a time, until the string runs straight again. Then it is untangled.
explain: «Mia untangled her hair after the bath.» The sentence tells you the knots were taken out. Untangled is the past form of untangle, so it shows the job is already finished.
explain: The word can also describe a problem. «The detective untangled the mystery in the last chapter.» The mystery was a muddle of clues, and now it makes sense. Ask yourself: has the muddle been sorted out? If yes, untangled fits.
fact: Untangle is a verb: you untangle a knot, a wire, or a piece of string.
fact: Untangled is the past form, so it tells you the job is already done.
fact: «Untangled» can describe hair or string that is free of knots and tidy.
fact: «Untangled» can also mean a problem or mystery has been made clear.
fact: To check your meaning, swap in "sorted out" or "free of knots" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Mia untangled her hair after the bath.» What does untangled mean here? | Cut off short | *Took the knots out | Washed twice | Dried with a towel
exercise: «The detective untangled the mystery in the last chapter.» What does untangled mean here? | *Made clear and worked out | Lost forever | Hidden under a rug | Broken into pieces
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to untangled? | Tied tight | Knotted | *Sorted | Tangled up
test: «The fishing line was untangled before the boat set off.» What does this sentence tell you? | The line was lost in the sea | The boat was too heavy to move | *The knots had been taken out and the line was ready | The line had snapped in two
test: «The fishing line was untangled before the boat set off.» Which word is the opposite of untangled? | Sorted | Straight | Clear | *Knotted
exam: Which sentence uses untangled to mean a problem was made clear? | *The riddle was untangled at last, and everyone understood it. | Dad untangled the garden hose. | The kite was untangled from the tree. | The puppy untangled its ball.
